 <p class="text-badge font-black text-brandOrange uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Key Takeaways</p>
 <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-4 speakable">Japan's PSE file has three layers: the product-safety mark, the importer's METI notification, and — for some designs — Radio Law Giteki. Match each layer to the product, factory, and sales route before the first shipment.</p>
 <ul class="text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
 <li><strong>PSE, METI notification, and Giteki are separate regimes.</strong> PSE is the product-safety mark; METI notification is the importer's business filing; Giteki is the Radio Law certification.</li><li><strong>AC adapters and DC power supplies are generally diamond PSE.</strong> A wireless charging pad may be round PSE depending on its construction; confirm the classification with a METI-registered CAB.</li><li><strong>The importer must file METI notification within 30 days.</strong> Each importer must file independently; one importer's notification does not cover another.</li><li><strong>December 25, 2025 and April 30, 2026 matter.</strong> The Specified Importer / Domestic Administrator rule applies to cross-border e-commerce; the J62368-1(2023) transition ends on April 30, 2026.</li><li><strong>The diamond certificate holder must be the actual factory.</strong> A trading company cannot hold it, and each manufacturing factory needs its own certificate.</li>
 </ul>
