<section id="verify-supplier" class="mb-16">
 <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">9. How to verify a supplier's PSE claim</h2>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">A supplier's "PSE certified" claim is a starting point, not a conclusion. Ask for the following:</p>
<ol class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-2 list-decimal pl-5"><li>Which PSE mark applies to this model — diamond or round — and why?</li><li>Who is the certificate holder? Is it the actual factory?</li><li>Which registered body issued the certificate, and what is the certificate number?</li><li>Which factory or factories are covered? Does each factory have its own certificate?</li><li>Which standard and edition: J62368-1(2020) or J62368-1(2023)?</li><li>Can you provide the duplicate certificate for our Japanese importer?</li><li>Does the label show our importer name and the registered body's name?</li><li>Does the product need Giteki? Which frequency band and radio module?</li><li>What test records will you provide, and for how long?</li><li>What changes trigger a new certificate or a change notification?</li></ol>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Red flags:</p>
<ul class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5"><li>A "PSE certificate" with no certificate number, no registered body, or no model/factory match.</li><li>A certificate holder that is a trading company rather than the factory.</li><li>One certificate presented as covering several factories.</li><li>A CE or FCC report presented as if it were a PSE certificate.</li><li>No standard edition or expiry date on the certificate.</li><li>No duplicate certificate for the importer.</li><li>A wireless charger with no answer on the radio band or Giteki scope.</li></ul>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Verification does not stop at the certificate PDF. Ask the registered body or check its public registry for the certificate number, the certificate holder, the factory, and the model. If the certificate covers a similar model, request the test report for the exact model and check the label artwork. A certificate that cannot be matched to the factory and the model is not a compliance file for your shipment.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">For a step-by-step check of FCC, UL, and CE documents, see our <a href="/blog/verify-fake-charger-certificates-fcc-ce-ul/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline">guide to verifying charger certificates</a>.</p>
<div class="bg-brandBlue/5 border-l-4 border-brandOrange rounded-r-xl p-6 mt-6"><p class="text-badge font-black text-brandOrange uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Factory-Side Note</p><blockquote class="text-slate-700 text-base italic leading-relaxed">The certificate holder must be the actual manufacturer. If a supplier cannot name the certificate holder and the factory in the same document, the file is not ready for a Japanese importer.</blockquote></div><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-8">
 <img src="/image/blog/how-to-choose-factory/wireless-charger-factory-quality-inspection.webp"
 alt="QC technician measuring a wireless charging pad with digital calipers during dimensional inspection at the factory"
 width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
 class="rounded-2xl shadow-lg w-full">
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>
<section id="cost-timeline" class="mb-16">
 <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">10. Cost and timeline: what drives the difference</h2>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">PSE cost is not one number. It depends on the category, the number of models and factories, the certificate validity period, and whether the product also needs Giteki or a Domestic Administrator.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">As a factory-side planning range, WOWOHCOOL's experience for a straightforward charger family is <strong>$1,000–2,500 and 3–5 weeks</strong> for the PSE work. That range is not a quote and not a universal benchmark. It can move when:</p>
<ul class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5"><li>the product is diamond rather than round;</li><li>the factory inspection covers multiple factories;</li><li>the certificate needs a longer validity period;</li><li>the product needs radio testing or Giteki;</li><li>the seller needs a Domestic Administrator and METI registration;</li><li>the certificate must be upgraded to J62368-1(2023);</li><li>retests are required after a design or component change.</li></ul>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Ask for a <strong>line-item quote</strong> that separates testing, factory inspection, certificate, duplicate certificate, radio testing, and the METI/JDR steps. A single "PSE price" hides the parts that determine whether the file is usable by the importer.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section id="next-steps" class="mb-16">
 <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
 <div class="bg-brandBlue/5 border-l-4 border-brandOrange p-6 rounded-r-xl">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">Next steps: match the mark and the importer route to the product</h2>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Japan is not a single-checkbox market. The compliance file has three layers:</p>
<ul class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5"><li><strong>Product safety:</strong> PSE, with the correct diamond or round classification.</li><li><strong>Importer status:</strong> METI notification, or Specified Importer registration with a Domestic Administrator for cross-border e-commerce.</li><li><strong>Radio:</strong> Giteki, if the product contains radio equipment.</li></ul>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Match each layer to the actual product, factory, and sales route before the first shipment. A certificate for a similar model, a CE report, or a Qi certificate is not a substitute for the Japanese file.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">If you are sourcing chargers for Japan, send your product specification, target market, and sales route. We will return a PSE/METI document checklist and the questions to send the factory.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>CTA:</strong> <a href="/service/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline">Talk to our OEM/ODM team</a> or <a href="/contact/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline">request a Japan compliance checklist</a>. You can also browse the <a href="/products/gan-charger/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline">GaN charger line</a>, <a href="/products/wireless-charger/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline">wireless charger line</a>, or <a href="/products/car-charger/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline">car charger line</a>.</p>
 </div>
