</section>

<section id="faq" class="mb-16">
 <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-8 text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-6 text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">The most common questions from brand owners and importers about Japan PSE, METI notification, and Giteki, answered with the rule and the importer duties that apply:</p>
 <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Does a charger need PSE in Japan?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Yes, if it is a mains-connected charger covered by DENAN. The product needs the applicable PSE mark, and the Japanese importer must notify METI and label the product. The mark type — diamond or round — depends on the product category and construction.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Is my charger diamond or round PSE?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">AC adapters and DC power supplies are generally Specified items (diamond PSE). A wireless charging pad may be Non-Specified (round) depending on its construction; the adapter, if separate, is generally Specified. Confirm the exact classification with a METI-registered conformity assessment body before printing a mark.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Does a Qi wireless charger need Giteki?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">It depends on the charging technology and whether the product contains a data radio. Basic Qi induction is often treated as outside the Radio Law; 6.78 MHz or 920 MHz wireless power transfer and Bluetooth/Wi-Fi modules are more likely to require MIC/Giteki approval. Confirm the scope with a registered certification body.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Can a Chinese factory hold the PSE certificate?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">For diamond PSE, the certificate holder must be the actual manufacturer (factory). A trading company or design house cannot hold it. If the model is produced in multiple factories, each factory needs its own certificate. The factory provides a duplicate certificate to the Japanese importer.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Is METI notification the same as PSE?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">No. PSE is the product safety mark and conformity process. METI notification is the importer&#x27;s business filing, due within 30 days of starting the import business. A product can have a PSE certificate and still be non-compliant if the importer has not notified METI or labeled the product correctly.</p>
</div>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

